==Battleground==
*1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
*3 [[Duche]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Prisoner Cat (Enemy)|Prisoner Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
**3 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
**3 [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
To begin the battle, spawn [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Erasers]] to stall the Doge Darks for a while, use other meatshields if they are pushing too hard. When you get to max money, begin to use a few cats. Enough that you get to the base, but not so much that they don't die. When you attack the base, let the Rain D. and Metal Doges get close to your base, then use rangers to destroy them. By the time they're all dead, Prisoner Cat should be near the base. Use tankers or rushers like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]], [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] to hit Prisoner Cat. Also spawn meatshields, [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island]], and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale]] for the Metal Doges. Repeat the process when the 2nd Rain D. spawns.

